<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9965" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">concussĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		id. (post-Aug.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a shaking, concussion.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vasorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 9,
					14 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">assidua facium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 4, 9, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vasta concussio quae duas suppressit urbes,</span>”
				<i>an earthquake</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 6, 25, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			jurid. Lat., <i>an extortion of money by means of
				threats</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 47, 13</span></i>: de concussione,
			several times; also <i><span class="en">Tert. ad Scap. 4
			sq.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
